9
00:38:52,799 --> 00:38:58,799
The French Dispatch of the Liberty, Kansas Evening Sun (or simply The French Dispatch) is a 2021 American anthology comedy drama film written,
directed, and co-produced by Wes Anderson from a story he conceived with Roman Coppola, Hugo Guinness, and Jason Schwartzman.

10
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
It features an expansive ensemble cast and follows three different storylines as the French news
bureau of the fictional Liberty, Kansas Evening Sun newspaper publishes its final issue.

11
00:47:31,199 --> 00:47:37,199
The first segment, "The Concrete Masterpiece", follows an incarcerated and unstable
painter, and stars Benicio del Toro, Adrien Brody, Tilda Swinton and Léa Seydoux.

12
00:51:50,399 --> 00:51:56,399
The second, "Revisions to a Manifesto", is inspired by the May 68 student protests,
and stars Frances McDormand, Timothée Chalamet, and Lyna Khoudri.

13
00:56:09,599 --> 00:56:15,599
The third, "The Private Dining Room of the Police Commissioner",  follows the kidnapping of a
police commissioner's son and stars Jeffrey Wright, Mathieu Amalric, and Stephen Park.

14
01:00:28,799 --> 01:00:34,799
Bill Murray also stars as Arthur Howitzer Jr., the paper's editor, while Owen Wilson appears in a
short segment that introduces the film's fictional setting of Ennui-sur-Blasé.

15
01:04:48,000 --> 01:04:54,000
The project was first mentioned in August 2018 as an
untitled musical set after World War II.

16
01:09:07,199 --> 01:09:13,199
That December, the film was officially announced, with
Anderson calling it a "love letter to journalists".

17
01:13:26,399 --> 01:13:32,399
Filming took place between November 2018 and March
2019, with cinematographer Robert D.

18
01:17:45,599 --> 01:17:51,599
Yeoman, in the city of Angoulême, France.

19
01:22:04,800 --> 01:22:10,800
In post-production, editing was completed by Andrew Weisblum
and the score was composed by Alexandre Desplat.

20
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
Following a delay from 2020, The French Dispatch premiered at the Cannes Film Festival on July 12, 2021, and
was theatrically released in the United States by Searchlight Pictures on October 22, 2021.

21
01:30:43,199 --> 01:30:49,199
It received generally positive reviews, with praise for its
score, production design, and performances.

22
01:35:02,399 --> 01:35:08,399
It has grossed $46 million worldwide against its budget of $25 million.

23
01:39:21,599 --> 01:39:27,599
The film explores themes of art collector,
journalist, small town, france, poison.

24
01:43:40,799 --> 01:43:46,799
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
